 # Kraus and Ertl Method
 
-Also called: Cycle handling in MPVO, Hardware compositing for visibility cycles
 
 ## Overview
-The Kraus and Ertl method is a technique for handling visibility cycles in convex meshes during cell projection volume rendering [S1, S2]. It addresses the problem where a global topological sort of cells is impossible due to cyclic visibility dependencies, yet a local sort exists for each pixel center [S1, S2]. It sets itself apart from standard MPVO by detecting these cycles and using special hardware compositing methods to scan-convert them, rather than failing or producing artifacts [S1, S2].
